{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/84417-a-day-in-the-death-of-a-hierarchy-wraith","id":84417,"title":"A Day in the Death of a Hierarchy Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-04T23:10:35-08:00","id":84417,"title":"A Day in the Death of a Hierarchy Wraith","content":"I'm almost 100% sure this topic has been visited in the past, most likely on the old White Wolf forums, but I'd like to put the question out there afresh.<br /> <br /> What is the average day like for a wraith in the Hierarchy?<br /> <br /> According to Wraith, all wraiths who are reaped by the Hierarchy are inducted into the Legions depending on their manner of snuffing it.<br /> Legions have both a military and civilian arm, and depending on what you're good at you are ushered into one of these positions.<br /> So far so easy.<br /> <br /> The problem arises when your player characters are Hierarchy wraiths, and that problem is 'free time'.<br /> The obvious answer to a wraith who wants to go about his own business is to make him a civilian at character creation. That way he doesn't have to worry about going on patrols, being posted off or such like.<br /> But it still begs the question of how much time does he have to himself?<br /> You don't get an option of whether you join a legion or not, so presumably you don't have any say whether you work a nine-to-five or not either.<br /> It seems highly unlikely that your character is going to be able to skip work because he has pressing business some place else and not expect to get punished.<br /> This leads to all sorts of problems when players wish to fulfill their own agendas, especially when those agendas are several days travel away or indeed smack bang in the middle of the Tempest.<br /> When the player announces he wants to set out on a quest to recover a relic deep in the Tempest, do we as storytellers pronounce &quot;you better ask your boss for some time off&quot; before allowing him to do so? Which also brings up the possibly humorous response of &quot;you've already had your allotted four weeks this year!&quot;<br /> <br /> Am I missing something in regards to how Hierarchy wraiths spend their deaths in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> Or is it really so troublesome and are characters better off being Renegades?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T00:20:38-08:00","id":84446,"title":"","content":"I think the distinction is, all wraiths are <i>nominally</i> part of a Legion. Not all wraiths are &quot;active duty,&quot;, and I would venture that the majority are only partially employed by their Legion, it at all. They're more just registered for the draft, so to speak. Given the population of the Underworld (even if it's only 10% of all people that die, that's 10% <i>since people have started dying</i>), I don't think Stygia had the funds or resources to keep them all busy. So they drift to the Guilds, or Renegade status, and some get smelted. So unless they're Reaped by a Legion and pressed into service (or something worse), I would guess they basically just kind of hang out.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T00:33:26-08:00","id":84450,"title":"","content":"The stupid Edit button isn't working for me. So, I got curious and went looking - supposedly, over 150,000 people die every day. Let's say 10% of them become wraiths. Even if we take a conservative estimate and and count only those that die in Stygian-held territory, say another (very conservative) 10%, that's 1500 new souls. Now, some of the become Drones, or immediately fall to Oblivion, or whatever. Even if we take half of that, it's still 750 new Wraiths <i>every day</i>, 5250 new Wraiths a week. I don't think your players are going to be missed by their commanding officer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T23:33:26-08:00","id":85138,"title":"","content":"Thanks Nothing.<br /> So it seems that I've been running Wraith within normal parameters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It always struck me as &quot;I'm sure this isn't right&quot; when dealing with Hierarchy wraiths.<br /> Your point of there are simply too many souls to give every one of 'um a job is a good one and something I've played as an unwritten fact.<br /> <br /> I suppose one could look at free-wraith existence in terms of the Roman Republic, and since Stygia was based on such it's only fitting.<br /> When war came every man was expected to do his job.<br /> <br /> I think I can put that nagging sensation that I wasn't playing it right to bed finally.<br /> Thanks again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T07:36:14-08:00","id":86004,"title":"","content":"Nothing, if your numbers are right and the vast majority of people who die and become wraiths are drones, then you've solved the &quot;where does all the stuff&quot; issue. Those drones become the stuff. And the Articifers are a jobs program...<br /> <br /> I don't have the numbers to hand but how many people in the World of Darkness have Willpower 6+, because that's what it takes to be a non-drone kinda wraith. I think there's some guidelines in Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:13:20-08:00","id":87064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/84417-a-day-in-the-death-of-a-hierarchy-wraith?p=86004#post86004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing, if your numbers are right and the vast majority of people who die and become wraiths are drones, then you've solved the &quot;where does all the stuff&quot; issue. Those drones become the stuff. And the Articifers are a jobs program... I don't have the numbers to hand but how many people in the World of Darkness have Willpower 6+, because that's what it takes to be a non-drone kinda wraith. I think there's some guidelines in Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nothing's post certainly brings credence to the Drones view. I love the idea that a huge proportion of Underworld material comes from 'those who don't know'. In this world there is a huge surplus of material. If they ain't complaining we might as well use it, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}